{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.borromean_channel_ne_r_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.borromean_channel_ne_r_star","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L160-L178","doc":"**Concrete refutation.**  In the physical regime (`h ≠ 0`, so `c₃ > 0`) the\nBrunnian channel closure `= c₃` never equals `r*·c₃` for the derived\n`r* ≈ 1.585 ≠ 1`.  The missing A=3 magnitude is not in the sub-link\ndecomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.borromean_channelClosure_eq_c3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.borromean_channelClosure_eq_c3","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L145-L158","doc":"**Concrete: the channel closure over the `𝓑₃` sub-links equals exactly `c₃`.**\nPlugging the derived Borromean triple trace\n`τ_Borr(h) = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶)/(h² + 4)` (GAP-A-4 closed form;\n`BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.tauBorromean`) into the three-unlink-pairwise +\ntriple channel closure reproduces the `#4364` near-miss deficit\n`1 − τ_Borr = h⁴(3 + h²)/(h² + 4)` — the `0.297 MeV`, `0.63× μ₃` value — with **no\nmagnitude factor**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channel_no_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channel_no_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L126-L139","doc":"**No magnitude (the refutation).**  The Brunnian sub-link channel closure\nequals the single Borromean deficit, so it reproduces a target `r*·c₃`\n(`c₃ = deficit τ₁₂₃`) with `r* ≠ 1` *only* in the degenerate `c₃ = 0`.  For the\nderived A=3 factor `r* = μ₃/c₃ ≈ 1.585 ≠ 1` and any nonzero deficit, the channel\ndecomposition cannot supply it: it contributes magnitude factor exactly `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_closures_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_closures_agree","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L114-L118","doc":"Under Brunnian triviality the additive and multiplicative closures agree —\nboth are the single Borromean deficit, no channel structure survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channelClosureMul_eq_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channelClosureMul_eq_triple","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**Brunnian collapse (multiplicative) — the decisive identity.**  With the\nthree pairwise deficits `= 0`, *every cross term of* `1 − ∏(1 − fᵢ)` *vanishes*\n(each factor `1 − fᵢ = 1`), so the multiplicative closure also equals the single\n3-body deficit.  This is why the interface-product's \"beyond-pairwise content\"\nsupplies nothing here: the pairwise factors are identically the unlink. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channelSumAdd_eq_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian_channelSumAdd_eq_triple","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**Brunnian collapse (additive).**  Every proper 2-sub-link of `𝓑₃` is the\nunlink (`τ₁₂ = τ₁₃ = τ₂₃ = 1`), so its deficit vanishes and the additive channel\nsum equals the single 3-body Borromean deficit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.channelClosureMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.channelClosureMul","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L91-L96","doc":"Multiplicative sub-link channel closure `1 − ∏ᵢ(1 − fᵢ)` (interface-product\n/ Ursell form).  Written verbatim in the `1 − ∏(1 − fᵢ)` shape so the cross-term\nstructure is visible; the pairwise cross terms are what Brunnian triviality\nkills. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.channelSumAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.channelSumAdd","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L87-L89","doc":"Additive sub-link channel sum over the three 2-sub-links + the triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.deficit","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanSubLinkChannelSum.lean#L82-L85","doc":"Normalized trace deficit of a sub-link against its unit unlink baseline\n(corpus convention, matches `BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.one_sub_tauBorromean`):\n`f = 1 − τ`.  So `τ = τ_unlink = 1 ⇒ f = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}